HTTP/2 fingerprinting extracted from https://github.com/Xetera/nginx-http2-fingerprint
(commit b44c3803b5b34431dc3c61078f30d8be5bcab3e9, based on nginx 1.21.2).
Ported to OpenResty 1.31.1.1's bundled nginx-1.31.1: only the fingerprint
collection points (SETTINGS / PRIORITY / WINDOW_UPDATE frames, pseudo-header
names in ngx_http_v2.c) and the $http2_fingerprint variable in
ngx_http_v2_module.c were kept; the upstream fork's other changes (request
body rework reverts, ssl_ciphers reordering) are unrelated to nginx 1.21.2
and were dropped. Differences from the original fork: fp allocation moved
before the c->buffer early-handler loop in ngx_http_v2_init (the buffer loop
invokes state handlers before the old insertion point, which would deref
fp == NULL on connections with a pre-read preface), and priority frames
record h2c->state.sid directly (state_priority no longer holds a stream).
Applied with patch -p1 inside bundle/nginx-1.*.

